Rewritten 2026-07-05 from the repo review; pruned the same day after
the first work wave landed. The 2018 list is fully absorbed by the
bartcore rewrite (see docs/design/); "warn on possible factors" is
retired as obsolete. DONE and removed from this list: the five
verified review bugs (gp zero weights, rbart_vi prior lookup by name,
silent weights recycling, chi-k Inf guard, dead-code/message cleanups;
bart2-vs-rbart_vi k handling resolved as deliberate - rbart forwards
through do.call so it must store the evaluated value), release
metadata (AC_INIT, SystemRequirements: C++20, .win header versions,
Description text), CI triggers for the bartcore branch +
workflow_dispatch, man-page examples for every headline feature,
logistic k/binaryOffset doc fixes, MIA and gp references, README
refresh with badge and package-authors note, and seven new coverage
test files (logistic+offset, DART x categorical x MIA, boundary
inputs, grouped weighted/binary halves + refusal, mutate-then-
serialize bitwise for all three leaf types, bridge errors, plot
smoke).

release
  push dbarts 1.0-0 (branch bartcore) and stan4bart 0.0-13; submit both
    to CRAN together
  stan4bart follow-up: adopt categorical splits (pins factors =
    "indicators"); lockstep with the dbarts release
  revdepcheck before submission: dbarts has CRAN reverse dependencies
    (stan4bart, bartCause, ...) and 1.0-0 deletes an ABI header - run
    revdepcheck::revdep_check(), coordinate the stan4bart lockstep
    upload, and write cran-comments.md documenting the break and the
    revdep status (no cran-comments.md exists)
  Windows-arm64 runs scalar kernels: the .win config headers never
    define COMPILER_SUPPORTS_NEON and Makevars.win's ARCH check has no
    aarch64 branch; consider a NEON branch
  verified clean by the build review: state mask serialization is
    byte-shifted (endian-safe); .Call registration complete; dbarts.h
    is C89-clean and matches the bridge; tarball free of build junk;
    sublibrary Makefiles own the SIMD source lists cross-platform

usability
  thread cancellation (2018 carryover, still real): nothing calls
    R_CheckUserInterrupt, so Ctrl-C during run() is deferred until the
    C call returns, single- and multi-chain alike. Needs a main-thread
    poll between iterations, a cooperative cancel flag the chains
    check, and worker joins before the error propagates; touches the
    hot loop, so speed and equivalence gates apply.
  weights + binary refusal fires at sampler creation in the bridge
    (good message, wrong layer); add an early R-side check.
  rbart_vi's sparse refusal doesn't say why or point at dbarts/bart2,
    which do support sparse.
  bart/bart2 lack xbart's up-front numeric argument validation
    (power/base/k ranges, counts); invalid values surface as opaque
    errors deep in parsePriors.

api surface
  xbart cannot reach DART or split.probs: cgm(power, base) is
    hardcoded (xbart.R:117) while dbarts/bart2/rbart_vi all expose it;
    xbart even exposes resid.prior, so the tree-prior gap looks
    unintentional.
  dbarts() has no seed argument; every convenience wrapper grew one
    and the base factory requires dbartsControl(rngSeed = ).
  no summary() method or credible-interval API; intervals are computed
    inline in plot.* and discarded. residuals.bart/.rbart hardcode
    fitted type "ev" - no link-scale residuals through the generic.
  plotTree is reachable only through the retained sampler
    ($fit$plotTree, $fit[[i]]$plotTree for multi-chain rbart);
    extract(type = "trees") wraps the chain indirection but plotTree
    has no fit-level dispatch. The rendering already handles linear
    and gp leaves.

performance (static hypotheses; measure before acting; suggested
order: pass fusion -> split bookkeeping -> custom-prior profiling ->
residual restructure)
  run-loop pass fusion, ORDER-PRESERVING: the per-tree sweep makes 8
    full O(n) passes (chain.hpp:371-373 residual build as
    memcpy+subtract+add, :420-426 fit swap as subtract+add+memcpy,
    plus setNodeAverages and the draw write). Fusing the residual
    build into one (y - total) + old loop and having the draw write
    the treeFits_ slab directly (dropping currFits_ and the trailing
    memcpy) is bitwise identical per element and cuts ~3 passes:
    ceiling ~10-15% of iteration time at n=10000. The bigger
    restructure - maintain R = y - totalFits across the sweep, ~3
    passes total, ~25% ceiling - is ORDER-CHANGING (totalFits carries
    FP accumulation history the state format preserves) and means
    re-recording the equivalence baselines.
  numVariablesAvailable does O(p x depth) ancestor re-walks per call
    (tree.hpp:386-391); growthProbability and the move preambles only
    need a boolean (early-exit), and drawSplitVariable can collect all
    per-variable intervals in one ancestor walk, O(p + depth). Both
    result-identical, ORDER-PRESERVING. 5-15% at p=10, grows with p -
    at DART-scale p this bookkeeping can dominate. change/swap also
    score whole-tree treeLogProbability twice per move where subtree
    differences cancel exactly (order-changing; likely subsumed).
  linear-leaf draw recomputes accumulateNodeStatistics the marginal
    just ran on the same node (model.hpp:275-333); caching the
    crossproduct across the score->draw gap is bitwise identical.
    Also setNodeAverages maintains constant-leaf stats linear leaves
    never read (skippable if constexpr). 10-25% of linear-leaf runs;
    zero effect on default runs.
  rbart_vi custom-prior R loop pays a full bridge round trip per
    posterior sample (rbart.R: setOffset + run(0L, 1L), ~10 fresh
    SEXPs per call in bartcore_run); built-in priors already bypass
    via in-core. Profile before touching; only that path pays.
  test-fit routing is serial over test rows (chain.hpp findBottom per
    row per tree); rows are independent chains so parallelizing is
    order-preserving - only matters when numTest ~ n.
  x86 SIMD is silently scalar: the SSE2/AVX bodies of
    misc_addVectorsInPlace, misc_subtractVectorsInPlace, and
    misc_setVectorToConstant contain scalar loops with the real
    intrinsics commented out (linearAlgebra_sse2.c:173-215 and
    siblings); dispatch tables and cpuid detection all wired; NEON
    arms live. Likely LOW impact - the scalar bodies autovectorize at
    -O2 on modern compilers - so either restore the intrinsics after
    measuring on x86 or simplify away the dead dispatch weight.
    misc_setIndexedVectorToConstant never entered the dispatch table
    at all. The SSR kernel has no SIMD leaf, unlike its mean/variance
    neighbors.
  threading: chains only (sampler.hpp std::thread); within-chain
    tree-level parallelism is structurally blocked by backfitting, and
    the observation-level htm machinery is dormant by design (all call
    sites pass a null manager, tree.hpp:407-409 - the serial unrolled
    accumulators are the fast path). Threaded reductions would change
    summation order and force baseline re-records. Verified clean: the
    hot loop has no allocation churn (scratch reused throughout).

internals
  chain.hpp opens the scalar/vector/function three-way if constexpr in
    ~12 methods (44 sites); hoisting per-shape helpers would make a
    fourth leaf shape touch one place instead of twelve. Large; the
    equivalence gate arbitrates.
  bridge: createHolder and bartcore_createFromHandle duplicate their
    parse/validate prologue; the binary-weights error string appears 4
    times; bartcore_run's hand-counted UNPROTECT(10) allocation
    cascade and getTrees' 240-line gather/emit both have clean
    extraction seams.
  bart/bart2/rbart_vi duplicate tree/resid-prior construction;
    extract a shared builder (note: the k slot must stay evaluated for
    rbart_vi's do.call forwarding and unevaluated for bart2's call
    redirection - the builder needs a switch).
  createClassicSampler (facade.hpp:315) now means "constant leaf" -
    rename; createSampler/createSamplerOverStore duplicate the
    designation validation loop.
  message polish leftovers: validateArgumentsInEnvironment hardcodes
    "dbarts" in messages shown from other callers.
  hardening: partitionFlatIndices shifts by an unvalidated test
    category code (tree.hpp:1316); every current caller validates
    first, but a one-line clamp makes the tree layer safe standalone.
  Makevars.win passes raw $(ARFLAGS) where Makevars.in has a -crs
    fallback; mirror or comment the asymmetry.

tests (remaining gaps from the coverage review)
  the equivalence gate now covers logistic, categorical, MIA, adaptive
    DART, linear/gp leaves, sparse, and exact-zero weights (eight added
    scenarios driven through the sampler API, baseline re-recorded at
    19c499a); grouped rbart_vi fits stay out - their multi-chain result
    shape does not fit the single-fit summary, so add a scenario only if
    a grouped refactor is planned.
  zero-weight fits for the constant and linear leaves still lack a
    targeted tinytest assertion (gp has the fix's regression tests); the
    equivalence zeroweights scenario exercises the constant-leaf
    no-likelihood path and the collapseEmptyNodes weightTotal > 0 guard
    on every gate run, but only bitwise against itself, not an oracle.
  post-mutation assertions are near-tautologies (is.finite only) in
    the older linear/gp mutation tests; the new mutate-then-serialize
    file covers the bitwise side, but comparing against a
    from-scratch sampler after mutation would strengthen the rest.
  MIA setPredictor that moves NA patterns on an incorporate sampler.

docs
  prose-level man-page pass before release: codoc mismatches are
    check-gated, prose drift is not (precedent: linear's stale
    "unavailable in xbart" survived until the gp landing).
  vignettes predate the rewrite: working_with_saved_trees.Rmd hangs
    its prose on seed = 2 "chosen to generate a deep tree" under the
    OLD engine's RNG stream (empty subsets degrade silently, not
    loudly); the mixture vignette's qualitative claims are
    realization-dependent too; neither mentions family, dart, sparse,
    missing, or the new leaf models. Re-run, re-pick seeds, re-verify
    prose.
  NEWS could consolidate an upgrade-path paragraph (the breaking
    changes are documented but scattered across bullets).

repo modernization (existing infra: r-lib R-CMD-check matrix now
running on the bartcore branch, .lintr, air.toml, Authors@R modern)
  add a sanitizer job (ASAN/UBSAN via the r-hub/rocker devel-san
    containers): a rewritten pointer-heavy C++ engine is exactly what
    CRAN's clang-san/gcc-san rebuilds bite; running it first is much
    cheaper than a CRAN bounce.
  run tests/cpp in CI alongside R CMD check; the equivalence gate can
    ride too but needs its statistical mode cross-platform (bitwise
    baselines are ARM-recorded; x86 SIMD changes last-ulp reduction
    order).
  coverage measurement: covr supports tinytest; wiring it to codecov
    (badge + CI job) turns the tests section above from one-time
    review findings into a tracked number.
  pkgdown site + GitHub Pages workflow: renders the man pages, NEWS,
    and both vignettes into a browsable home for the 1.0-0 feature
    set; near-zero maintenance once configured.
  enforce .lintr/air in CI or drop them: both configs exist but
    nothing runs them, so they silently rot.
  optional, larger, taste-dependent: roxygen2 migration (hand-written
    Rd is complete and codoc-clean today; migration buys inline
    doc-next-to-code at the cost of a huge one-time diff);
    NEWS.md instead of inst/NEWS.Rd (pkgdown renders it natively).

decision-gated (design notes in docs/design/)
  sampled gp lengthscales: gp-leaves.md stage-4 addendum - needs a
    theta prior choice, per-sample theta channels in state/flatten
    formats, and costs multiples of the draw phase per sweep; not the
    mechanical follow-up the original proposal suggested
  public group.by exposure beyond rbart_vi: grouped-random-effects.md;
    naming reserved

consumer-gated
  sparse extensions (sparse-columns.md landing notes): in-place
    mutation, sparse x.test, u8 per-column widths, streaming range
    kernel, mutation on dense-backed mixed columns
  low-rank gp kernels
  score-to-draw chol(V) reuse within a sweep (measured second-order
    after the kernel cache)
